{
    "background_story": "McSteamy, aka Dr. Eric Thompson, was a brilliant and rugged orthopedic surgeon with a secret passion for carpentry. In his free time, he loved to tinker with woodworking projects, and his trusty mallet was always by his side. With a few swift swings, he could drive a nail home with precision and finesse. McSteamy's colleagues at Grey Sloan Memorial Hospital often joked that his surgical skills were rivaled only by his carpentry prowess. Little did they know, the mallet had been passed down from his grandfather, a master craftsman, and held sentimental value. McSteamy's love for woodworking was not just a hobby, but a way to connect with his heritage and clear his mind after a long day of saving lives.",
